why Every Horde quest of Scarlet Monastery's four wings, lead-ins included.

# Scarlet Monastery's Horde quests in one guide: the pick-ups in the
# Undercity and Thunder Bluff, the Test of Lore chain through Thousand Needles,
# Stonetalon and Ashenvale (for Mages their Rituals of Power chain too), the
# four wings one after the other, then the hand-ins. Steps already done are
# passed over, so the guide picks up wherever the chain stands.
#
# The quests: Varimathras' 1048 Into The Scarlet Monastery (Loksey, Herod,
# Mograine, Whitemane); for characters who handed in Going, Going, Guano! (1109,
# Razorfen Kraul), Faranell's 1113 Hearts of Zeal; Dorn Plainstalker's 1149
# Test of Faith -> 1150 Test of Endurance -> 1151 Test of Strength -> 1152 Test
# of Lore (to Braug Dimspirit) -> 1154 -> 6627 -> 1159 (to Parqual Fintallas)
# -> 1160 (Beginnings of the Undead Threat, in the Library) -> 6628; Sage
# Truthseeker's 1049 Compendium of the Fallen (for Orcs, Tauren and Trolls);
# Vorrel Sengutz' 1051 Vorrel's Revenge (taken inside; the ring from Nancy
# Vishas, for Monika Sengutz). Mages: 1947 Journey to the Marsh -> Tabetha's
# 1949 -> Magus Tirth's 1950 -> 1951 Rituals of Power (in the Library).
#
# Left out: the Rogues' 78676 The Eye of Bhossca (its chain needs Shadowfang
# Keep); the Mages' 1952 Mage's Wand (it also needs Tabetha's 1948 Items of
# Power, outside this chain); 1394, Test of Lore's next step.
#
# Inside: nothing in the data places the bosses, Vorrel or the books inside,
# so their goals stand at the monastery's door (@82.6,33.8, Tirisfal) with
# `group 5`. The wings come in the client's group finder's level order
# (Graveyard 30-38, Library 33-41, Armory 36-44, Cathedral 38-46), each its own
# instance with its own door in the courtyard, and the bosses in the client's
# dungeon journal's order within them; my own runs met them that way, wing by
# wing. Every quest goal is counted by the quest log, so a group that takes
# them in another order still gets each step ticked.
#
# Sources (facts only):
# - Quests, NPCs, items, objects and rewards: Polestar's reference data
#   (data/forever, built from QuestieDB Forever 1.1.4) and Polestar 0.4.1.1's
#   Codex page for the dungeon. The leap, the answers and Parqual's last test
#   are the data's spots for those objectives.
# - The door: players' recordings, as Polestar's Codex holds them
#   (data/codex/entrances.json).
# - Runs of my own on 2026-11-14 and 15 (Horde, level 36 to 38), recorded with
#   Polestar's recorder: the Graveyard (Vishas, then Thalnos), the Library
#   (Loksey, then Doan, the Test of Lore and Compendium books), the Armory
#   (Herod) and the Cathedral, each entered through its own door; the Hearts
#   of Zeal from the Scarlet all through.
# - The wings and their levels: the client's group finder; the bosses: its
#   dungeon journal (as Polestar's Codex page holds it).
# - Mob levels from data/forever set the waits: Grenka Bloodscreech 31,
#   Rok'Alim the Pounder 30 (an elite), Nancy Vishas 33 (an elite).

